{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-18763","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17193","text":"Dual- and Triple-Loop Machine Architecture"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-18765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17194","marks":["bold"],"text":"PULSE update (OS-010, 2026-04):"},{"id":"spn-17195","text":" With the introduction of OS-010 PULSE, the loop-interlock pattern documented here is now formalized as a manifest standard. Graphonomous, PRISM, AgenTroMatic, and every other portfolio loop declare their phases in "},{"id":"spn-17196","marks":["code"],"text":"<loop>.pulse.json"},{"id":"spn-17197","text":" files (see "},{"id":"spn-17198","marks":["code"],"text":"/PULSE/manifests/"},{"id":"spn-17199","text":"), validated against "},{"id":"spn-17200","marks":["code"],"text":"pulse-loop-manifest.v0.1.json"},{"id":"spn-17201","text":". The \"dual loop\" is a special case of arbitrarily nestable PULSE loops — the same machine grouping works at any depth, and PRISM's "},{"id":"spn-17202","marks":["code"],"text":"interact"},{"id":"spn-17203","text":" phase reads the inner system's PULSE manifest to discover the "},{"id":"spn-17204","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-17205","text":" boundary at runtime rather than hard-coding the integration. See \"Triple loop and beyond\" below."}]}],"id":"blk-18764","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-18766","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17206","text":"The Problem"}]},{"id":"blk-18767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17207","text":"Graphonomous exposes 29 MCP tools. PRISM specifies 47. When both run in the same session (the benchmarking use case), the client sees 76 tools. Research shows:"}]},{"id":"blk-18768","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-18770","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17208","text":"Tool selection accuracy degrades past ~30 tools (Opus 4: 49% correct at that scale)"}]}],"id":"blk-18769","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-18772","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17209","text":"Each tool definition consumes 500–2,000 tokens of context before conversation starts"}]}],"id":"blk-18771","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-18774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17210","text":"76 tools can burn 40–80K tokens just on schema overhead"}]}],"id":"blk-18773","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-18775","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17211","text":"The Insight: Machine Around the Loop, Not the Category"}]},{"id":"blk-18776","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17212","text":"Instead of grouping tools by what they "},{"id":"spn-17213","marks":["italic"],"text":"touch"},{"id":"spn-17214","text":" (graph write, graph read, belief, etc.), group them by "},{"id":"spn-17215","marks":["bold"],"text":"which phase of the closed loop the agent is in"},{"id":"spn-17216","text":" when it calls them."}]},{"id":"blk-18777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17217","text":"Both Graphonomous and PRISM are closed-loop systems. Their loops are structurally parallel and interlock when PRISM evaluates Graphonomous:"}]},{"id":"blk-18778","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Graphonomous (memory loop)          PRISM (evaluation loop)\n──────────────────────────          ───────────────────────\nretrieve  \"What do I know?\"         compose    \"What should I test?\"\nroute     \"What should I do?\"       interact   \"Run the test\"\nact       \"Do it\"                   observe    \"Judge the result\"\nlearn     \"Did it work?\"            reflect    \"What should change?\"\nconsolidate \"Clean up\"              diagnose   \"What's actionable?\""},{"id":"blk-18779","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17218","text":"Graphonomous: 29 tools → 5 machines"}]},{"id":"blk-18780","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17219","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve"},{"id":"spn-17220","text":" — \"What do I know?\""}]},{"id":"blk-18781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17221","text":"The agent calls this when it needs context before reasoning or acting."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-18783","spans":[{"id":"spn-17222","text":"Action"}]},{"id":"blk-18784","spans":[{"id":"spn-17223","text":"Replaces"}]},{"id":"blk-18785","spans":[{"id":"spn-17224","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-18782","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-18786","spans":[{"id":"spn-17225","marks":["code"],"text":"context"}]},{"id":"blk-18787","spans":[{"id":"spn-17226","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"}]},{"id":"blk-18788","spans":[{"id":"spn-17227","text":"κ-aware ranked retrieval with topology annotations"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18789","spans":[{"id":"spn-17228","marks":["code"],"text":"episodic"}]},{"id":"blk-18790","spans":[{"id":"spn-17229","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_episodic"}]},{"id":"blk-18791","spans":[{"id":"spn-17230","text":"Time-range filtered episodic nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18792","spans":[{"id":"spn-17231","marks":["code"],"text":"procedural"}]},{"id":"blk-18793","spans":[{"id":"spn-17232","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_procedural"}]},{"id":"blk-18794","spans":[{"id":"spn-17233","text":"Semantic search scoped to procedural nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18795","spans":[{"id":"spn-17234","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage"}]},{"id":"blk-18796","spans":[{"id":"spn-17235","marks":["code"],"text":"coverage_query"}]},{"id":"blk-18797","spans":[{"id":"spn-17236","text":"Standalone epistemic coverage (act/learn/escalate)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18798","spans":[{"id":"spn-17237","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence"}]},{"id":"blk-18799","spans":[{"id":"spn-17238","marks":["code"],"text":"trace_evidence_path"}]},{"id":"blk-18800","spans":[{"id":"spn-17239","text":"Weighted Dijkstra evidence path between nodes"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18801","spans":[{"id":"spn-17240","marks":["code"],"text":"frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-18802","spans":[{"id":"spn-17241","marks":["code"],"text":"epistemic_frontier"}]},{"id":"blk-18803","spans":[{"id":"spn-17242","text":"Wilson interval uncertainty analysis"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-18804","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-17243","marks":["code"],"text":"route"},{"id":"spn-17244","text":" — \"What should I do?\""}]},{"id":"blk-18805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-17245","text":"The agent calls this to decide whether to act, learn, deliberate, or escalate."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-18807","spans":[{"id":"spn-17246","text":"Action"}]},{"id":"blk-18808","spans":[{"id":"spn-17247","text":"Replaces"}]},{"id":"blk-18809","spans":[{"id":"spn-17248","text":"Description"}]}],"id":"blk-18806","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-18810","spans":[{"id":"spn-17249","marks":["code"],"text":"topology"}]},{"id":"blk-18811","spans":[{"id":"spn-17250","marks":["code"],"text":"topology_analyze"}]},{"id":"blk-18812","spans":[{"id":"spn-17251","text":"SCC/κ analysis with routing recommendation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18813","spans":[{"id":"spn-17252","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-18814","spans":[{"id":"spn-17253","marks":["code"],"text":"deliberate"}]},{"id":"blk-18815","spans":[{"id":"spn-17254","text":"κ-driven deliberation over cyclic regions"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18816","spans":[{"id":"spn-17255","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"}]},{"id":"blk-18817","spans":[{"id":"spn-17256","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_survey"}]},{"id":"blk-18818","spans":[{"id":"spn-17257","text":"Priority survey across active goals"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18819","spans":[{"id":"spn-17258","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_cycle"}]},{"id":"blk-18820","spans":[{"id":"spn-17259","marks":["code"],"text":"attention_run_cycle"}]},{"id":"blk-18821","spans":[{"id":"spn-17260","text":"Full triage → dispatch attention cycle"}]}],[{"id":"blk-18822","spans":[{"id":"spn-17261","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-18823","spans":[{"id":"spn-17262","marks":["code"],"text":"review_goal"}]},{"id":"blk-18824","spans":[{"id":"spn-17263","text":"Coverage-driven act/learn/escalate gate"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-18825","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-172